    Rights audit for eight held videos, new original piano piece, fix sample pitch
    
    Audit: every song in x03-x08 and w01/w02/w04 was matched note by note against
    the scores it could have come from. Most melodies and chord symbols are
    identical to Paul Hardy's Xmas Tunebook (CC BY-NC-SA), and Vivaldi's Winter is
    Mutopia CC BY-SA 3.0, so all eight need permission or replacement. Source
    pages and licence texts retrieved today are kept in data/licenses.
    
    orig01_winter_reading_piano: newly composed piece in F (intro, A, A', B in D
    minor, bridge, A'', coda), rendered with the Iowa piano; 3-minute preview,
    FLAC master, MIDI, QA results, Shorts cues and a visual brief for GPT.
    
    Fixes found while making it: samples were saved at 48 kHz but played at
    44.1 kHz, so every recorded instrument sounded about 1.47 semitones flat;
    prepare_piano_samples.py now saves at the engine rate. Piano samples are
    levelled against their neighbours (the recordings differ by up to 14 dB from
    note to note).
    
